# Environment variables for Wynko's Supabase Edge Functions.
#
# These are NOT read from a repo-root .env file — Supabase Edge
# Functions get their env vars from project-level function secrets
# (Supabase Dashboard → Edge Functions → Manage secrets, or
# `supabase secrets set KEY=value` via the CLI), shared across every
# function in the project. This file exists purely as documentation
# of what needs to be set there. Never put real values in this file
# or in any .env file that gets committed.
#
# The frontend (home.html, shared.js, etc.) doesn't use env vars at
# all — it hardcodes SUPABASE_URL and the anon key directly in
# src/lib/supabase.js. That's intentional and safe: the anon key is
# meant to be public, and every table has RLS enabled (verified).

# --- Supabase (used by nearly every function) ---
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# NOTE — naming inconsistency found in the currently-deployed functions:
# close-study-day, award-milestone-coins, resolve-challenge,
# resolve-gvg-challenge, evaluate-group-leadership, and
# evaluate-group-verified all read Deno.env.get("SERVICE_ROLE_KEY")
# (no SUPABASE_ prefix) instead of SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY. Since
# Supabase secrets are shared project-wide, either both names are set
# to the same value right now (redundant but working), or the
# SERVICE_ROLE_KEY-only functions have been silently failing since
# deploy. Worth confirming which in the Supabase dashboard, then
# standardizing every function on SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY so this
# can't happen again.
SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# --- Cron-triggered functions (close-study-day, award-milestone-coins,
#     resolve-challenge, resolve-gvg-challenge, evaluate-group-leadership,
#     evaluate-group-verified, schedule-tick) ---
# Shared secret checked against the x-cron-secret header, so these
# endpoints can't be triggered by anyone who doesn't have it.
CRON_SECRET=

# --- ai-generate-schedule, ai-manage-blocks (AI timetable / AI block manager) ---
GEMINI_API_KEY=
GEMINI_MODEL=

# --- agora-token (voice call tokens for study rooms) ---
# App ID is not secret on its own, but the certificate must never be
# client-side — it's what lets someone mint a valid token without one.
AGORA_APP_ID=
AGORA_APP_CERTIFICATE=

# --- admob-ssv-callback (rewarded-ad server-side verification) ---
# No secret env var — verifies Google's signed callback using Google's
# own rotating public keys fetched at request time, not a shared secret.
